{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310706,"nonce":"QT7VI0eXzinwQ/IXhhtMMmZ74t0=","title":"FIXED — `e.details()` missing \"Called from\" frames because `enable_stack_traces` was force-disabled in both Application preset and ...","message":"`test_exception_method_parity` printed `hasStack=false` because `e.details()` returned just `\"boom\"` instead of `\"Exception: \\\"boom\\\"\\n\u003cframes\u003e\"`. The Throw lowering's stack-capture call was working; the runtime flag controlling whether the capture returned a real string was off.\n\n\nTwo places force-disabled `enable_stack_traces`:\n\n1. [compiler/src/codegen/tiered_backend.rs:616](compiler/src/codegen/tiered_backend.rs#L616) — `TierPreset::Application` had `enable_stack_traces: false` with a comment `// TEMP: disabled to test global store bug`. The referenced bug was fixed long ago.\n\n2. [src/main.rs:1223](src/main.rs#L1223) — `run_file` unconditionally overwrote `config.enable_stack_traces = false` AFTER reading the preset, so even a corrected preset would be silenced.\n\nTogether these meant `is_enabled()` (checked by `rayzor_native_stack_trace_call_stack`) returned false. The Throw handler still STORED the result, but the result was an empty string — hence `e.stack == \"\"` and `details()` took the early `return message;` branch.\n\n\n* Re-enable `enable_stack_traces: true` in `TierPreset::Application`.\n* Replace the unconditional override in `run_file` with `if release { config.enable_stack_traces = false; }` so release builds still skip the instrumentation overhead and debug runs honour the preset.\n\n\nThe runtime path is already complete (Throw handler populates the field; `details()` formats it; `rayzor_set_stack_traces_enabled` toggles capture). Any future regressions where `e.stack` is empty in debug mode should check (1) preset and (2) any subsequent `config.enable_stack_traces = false` overrides before assuming the capture itself is broken.\n\nVerification: full suite 128/128 over two consecutive runs. `test_exception_method_parity` now prints `hasStack=true` plus formatted \"Called from Main.thrower (...)\" frames.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_stack_traces_disabled` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}